            <div xml:id="d98">

                <pb facs="0103" n="94" sameAs="frus:frus1940v02/pg94"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">340.1115A/622c: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the
                        Minister in Ireland</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                            >Gray</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1940-05-16T17:00:00-04:00">May 16, 1940—5
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>14. London is being authorized to advise American citizens to proceed to Eire as
                    a place of greater safety under existing circumstances. London will communicate
                    with you and will probably indicate approximate number of evacuees. Please
                    notify consuls and exercise agencies at your command to render assistance to
                    evacuees that they may secure lodgings in cities or in countryside at their own
                    expense and advise Department as to number of such persons in Eire.</p>
                <p>Department will consider advisability of sending a ship to a west coast port with
                    the idea of making available to them facilities direct to the United States at
                    their own expense.</p>
                <p>Detailed instructions will be sent in due course.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
